'' Two overloads with one signature are a duplicate definition (fbc error 4). Over BYDESC
'' parameters the array RANK decides: '()' is unknown rank and collides with any, two
'' known ranks collide only when equal. A definition of an already-declared overload is
'' not a second one, and neither is a pair differing in element or result type.
''
'' ONLY A PAIR WITH A BYDESC PARAMETER IS JUDGED -- the general scalar case produced 13
'' false rejections over the 1222 fbc-accepted files (cross-namespace overload chains, and
'' the CRT headers' _rotl family). Matches fbc on lines 18 and 21.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/duplicate-bydesc-overload.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' GOLDEN: expected/duplicate-bydesc-overload.out
